//! Partial 1-to-1 port of `src/codegen/exprs/ptr-fns.ts`.
//!
//! Currently exposes one pure formatter:
//!
//!   - `format_address_of(arg_code)` — wraps an already-generated C
//!     expression in the `(&...)` address-of form. This is the tail
//!     fallback path of `generateAddressOf` (the path that doesn't
//!     intercept array-index-range / slice-construction / function-
//!     pointer special cases). Pure string transformation.
//!
//! The slice-construction, array-index-range, and function-pointer
//! paths still depend on `context.sliceStructTypes`, the recursive
//! `generateExpr` dispatcher, and
//! `is_function_value_with_only_builtin_yo_inline_function_call` —
//! none of which are ported yet. The rvalue-spilling path
//! (taking the address of a function call by spilling to a temp)
//! depends on `get_variable_type_string` (✓ available) plus a fresh
//! temp counter that lives on the codegen context (not yet exposed
//! in yo-self), so it also waits.
open(import("std/string"));
/// Format the C address-of expression `(&arg_code)` — TS
/// `return `(&${argCode})`;` in `generateAddressOf`. Pure string
/// wrap; no codegen context needed.
format_address_of :: (fn(arg_code : String) -> String)({
  s := String.from("(&");
  s.push_str(arg_code.as_str());
  s.push_str(")");
  s
});
export(format_address_of);
